{"author":{"id":"a51b5961cc6de343a64125d8eb6a0f965aa434020b9c46ed932a1bbf143eb532"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791563178,"nonce":"EjfWCc4dYrs5JKHAPcM7GTwjCj0=","title":"Full CSS box model on layout nodes, and incremental child operations","message":"LayoutStyle covers 14 properties (sizes, direction, align, justify, overflow, grow, shrink, gap, a single padding). A framework needs the whole box model: margin, padding and border per side, position (relative, absolute) and inset, flex-wrap, align-self and align-content, flex-basis, order, display (flex, grid, none), grid templates and placement, aspect-ratio, overflow per axis, percentages and auto.\n\nblinc_abi already routes every one of these for the HashLink adapter (layout_router.rs, by property id, including grid parsing in grid.rs), and ashui sets them all. Bind that router to the owned LayoutContext and expose it, rather than growing the typed subset field by field: the CSS cascade (blinc_abi 449ad47) and the host interface's setProperty write through the same path, and a typed TypeScript style object can sit on top for those who build styles in code.\n\nAlso: insertBefore, append, removeChild and move on the native tree, so a framework's keyed list updates do not rebuild a parent's child list (setChildren stays for whole replacement). Writes coalesce per tick (d1a4fbe).","files":null}]}